   "source": [
    "#### Methodology\n",
    "\n",
    "**Determining Base Lactation Curve Parameters** (`set_lactation_parameters`) \n",
    "\n",
    "The Wood’s lactation curve parameters are initialized with base values \n",
    "retrieved from `lactation_inputs[\"parameter_mean_values\"]` in `LACTATION_CURVE_ADJUSTMENT_INPUTS.json`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Adjusting parameters** (`_calculate_adjusted_wood_parameters`) \n",
    "\n",
    "Wood's lactation curve parameters are adjusted based on temporal, geographical, \n",
    "and management factors [@Li_2022]. Each parameter (l, m, n) is adjusted using a series of modifications:\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-1}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.1**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{l}_\\text{adjusted} = \\text{l} + \\sum \\text{adjustments} \n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-2}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.2**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{m}_\\text{adjusted} = \\text{m} + \\text{scaling factor}_\\text{m} \\times \\sum \\text{adjustments} \n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-3}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.3**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{n}_\\text{adjusted} = \\text{n} + \\text{scaling factor}_\\text{n} \\times \\sum \\text{adjustments} \n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "$$ \n",
    "\\text{scaling factor}_\\text{m} = 10^{-2}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{scaling factor}_\\text{m} = 10^{-4}\n",
    "$$ \n",
    "\n",
    "Adjustments are applied based on:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Region (using FIPS codes): `_get_region_adjustments` \n",
    "* Year of simulation (adjusted for trends in milk production): `_get_year_adjustments`\n",
    "* Milking frequency (twice vs. thrice daily): `_get_milking_frequency_adjustments`\n",
    "* Parity (different lactation curves for different parities): `animal_parity`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Fitting Parameters to Target Milk Yield** (`_adjust_lactation_curve_to_milk_yield`) \n",
    "\n",
    "If `annual_milk_yield` is provided, the l parameter is optimized to match the expected 305-day milk yield:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Estimate herd average 305-day milk yield:\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-4}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.4**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Milk Yield}_{305} = \\frac{\\text{Annual Milk Yield}}{\\text{Number of Milking Cows}} \\times \\frac{305}{\\text{Days per year}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "* Estimate parity specific 305-day milk yield: (`_estimate_305_day_milk_yield_by_parity`)\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-5}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.5**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "M305_{Herd} = (M305_{P1} \\times P1\\%) + (M305_{\\text{P2}} \\times P2\\%) + (M305_{P3} times P3^+\\%)\n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-6}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.6**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "M305_{P2} = M305_{P1} \\times 118\\%\n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-7}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.7**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "M305_{P3^+} = M305_{P1} \\times 125\\%\n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.callout-note}\n",
    "118% and 125% are assumptions made based on the work by @Li_2022.\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "* Fit l Parameter Using Optimization: (`_fit_wood_l_param_to_milk_yield`). The error function is defined as: (`_calculate_305_day_milk_yield_error`)\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-8}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.8**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Error} = \\text{Predicted MilkYield305} - \\text{Target MilkYield305}\n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "Using Scipy's minimize function, the l parameter is iteratively adjusted to minimize this error.\n",
    "        \n",
    "* Final Lactation Curve Parameter Mapping. Once adjustments are made, parameters are stored in:\n",
    "\n",
    "`_parity_to_parameter_mapping` =   \n",
    "1: \"l\": ..., \"m\": ..., \"n\": ...,   \n",
    "2: \"l\": ..., \"m\": ..., \"n\": ...,   \n",
    "3: \"l\": ..., \"m\": ..., \"n\": ...  \n",
    "\n",
    "Equations below are not in the `LactationCurve` class, but they are useful to understanding the bigger picture of how lactation curve parameter estimates \n",
    "are generated in RuFaS. Please see the Milk Production section for more details on these equations [@Wood1967].\n",
    "\n",
    "**Wood's Lactation Curve**\n",
    "\n",
    "[See [AN.MLK-9](#eq-an-mlk-9)]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Y_t = l * t^{m} * e^{-nt}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "        \n",
    "Where:\n",
    "* Y(t): Daily milk yield\n",
    "* t: Time in days\n",
    "* l, m, n: Parameters adjusted for farm-specific conditions\n",
    "\n",
    "**305-Day Milk Yield**\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#eq-an-mlk-10}\n",
    "[[**AN.MLK.10**]]{.aside .content-visible when-format=\"html\"}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\int_{l}^{305} lt^me^{-nt}dt\n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {#sec-an-cull}\n",
    "### Culling\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "This section describes the processes of animals leaving the herd in RuFaS. Reasons for leaving the herd are death or sale. \n",
    "\n",
    "Sale may occur of:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Calves: all male calves; female calves based on `keep_female_calf_rate`\n",
    "* Heifer IIs: if the heifer does not have a successful conception or pregnancy and age (days born) exceeds `heifer_repro_cull_time`\n",
    "* Heifer IIIs: if cow herd does not have room for additional heifers\n",
    "* Cows (through two possible mechanisms): \n",
    "   * Disease-related culling, determined by a statistical distribution of occurrence, or\n",
    "   * Production-related culling, which occurs when a cow has been labeled “Do Not Breed” due to reproductive failure past a designated \n",
    "   number of days in milk and then her milk production drops below a designated threshold\n",
    "\n",
    "Deaths that may occur:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Cows: determined by a statistical distribution of occurrence \n",
    "* Stillborn calves \n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.callout-note}\n",
    "Stillborn calves are currently combined with calves sold at birth and reported as “calves sold”. \n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "Information about death and sale events are tracked and aggregated daily, including the day of death or sale, body weight, cull reason, days in milk, and parity. \n",
    "\n",
    "#### Required User Inputs"
   ]
